Restore Audacity 3.7.9 default shortcuts on Audacity 4 action names

Audacity 4 renamed many actions. The shipped shortcuts.xml still bound
keys to the old names, so familiar AU3 bindings never fired. This patch
rewires those sequences onto the live AU4 action keys and restores a
few AU3-default chords that AU4 left unbound.

Action-key remaps (old → new):
  - contrast-analyser → contrast-analyzer
  - sel-prev-clip → select-previous-clip
  - sel-next-clip → select-next-clip
  - split-new → split-into-new-track
  - preferences → preference-dialog
  - track-close → track-delete
  - skip-sel-start → skip-to-selection-start
  - skip-sel-end → skip-to-selection-end

Sequences restored or reassigned to match AU3 habits:
  - Ctrl+Y redo (in addition to Ctrl+Shift+Z)
  - Ctrl+K delete
  - Ctrl+P preferences (in addition to Ctrl+,)
  - F11 fullscreen
  - Ctrl+M add-label-playing (in addition to Ctrl+.)
  - Ctrl+Alt+X cut-leave-gap
  - Ctrl+Alt+K delete-leave-gap
  - Shift+R record-on-new-track
  - Ctrl+Shift+X expand-all-tracks (moved off cut-per-track-ripple)
  - Ctrl+F2 moved from accessibility-dev-show-tree onto its AU4 home

See patches/KEYBINDS.md for the full rationale.

Apply against an Audacity 4.x tree:
  git apply 0002-restore-audacity-3.7.9-default-shortcuts.patch

